  "description": "Josh Allen got zero Division I scholarship offers out of high school. In 2025 he signed a 330 million dollar deal.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Josh Allen (quarterback): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josh_Allen_(quarterback)\n\nFrom Wikipedia (Josh Allen): he received no scholarship offers from any NCAA Division I program; he grew up on a cotton farm near Firebaugh, California; he played one season at Reedley College, a junior college (2014), throwing 25 touchdowns with only 4 interceptions after becoming the starter; only Eastern Michigan and Wyoming offered a scholarship, and Eastern Michigan withdrew; the Bills drafted him seventh overall in the 2018 NFL draft and he signed a four-year, fully guaranteed $21 million contract; he won the NFL MVP award (announced February 6, 2025); on March 9, 2025 he signed a six-year extension worth $330 million, of which $250 million guaranteed, the largest guaranteed money ever given to an NFL player at the time of signing. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #joshallen #buffalobills #howtheymakemoney",
